{
 "_note": "Plan A.34 (Doug, 2026-10-07): an aggregate card is a hub. Every member opens its node -- a figure opens the whole symbol in the verse's words, which is the gateway to what the passage says it is (Doug: \"breastplate of righteousness is a gateway to righteousness\"): the concept, image, object or title the graph already holds where it is the same thing, a new one ('make') where none exists (Doug, 2026-10-07: \"there should be concept or image nodes for all the members\"; \"those should be consolidated as well\"); every move is a verb the passage gives and opens its verse. Labels are the Berean's words, with the text's capitals. ontology/interest-taxonomy.json (Microsoft Copilot's, 2026-09-13) keeps its ids, lists and shapes unchanged; this file is what the card shows instead. An existing node is reused only where that card is the same thing in the same sense, judged against the original (the Greek decides between translations: Gal 5:22's 'kindness' is chresotes, which the KJV called 'gentleness'). 'changed' says what the taxonomy listed that the passage does not hold, and why. A list with no graph card gets one ('make_card'): one card per list. tools/aggregate_nodes.py writes the made nodes and the list-to-member links.",
 "_reader": "Claude Opus 5.5, reading each passage in the Berean and the original, 2026-10-07",
